  "prefLabel": "Res 207.03 Scheduling of Hearing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Res 207.03 Scheduling of Hearing. Unless otherwise provided for by statute or rule, hearings shall be scheduled as soon as practicable following the events giving rise to the necessity for such hearing. The date set for the hearing shall allow sufficient and reasonable time for preparation of the case by the department and all parties.\n\nSource. #7568-A, eff 10-1-01, EXPIRED: 7-1-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/res200.html"
